{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xxv", "label": "Article XXV \u2014 Amendment procedure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_stage", "label": "Stage 29 \u2014 Noting a logical fallacy (planned, not started)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Planned, not built. A meme can be factually unimpeachable and still be a straw man, so today the part of a statement that does the persuading passes unremarked. Described as the most easily abused thing yet proposed here: icons are read as verdicts."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_three_failures", "label": "A fallacy is not a refutation, attaches to a passage, and is not a ruling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An argument can be badly made and its conclusion still true, so the page says so where the note is and no note changes a state, probability or trace. The anchor is a quoted, hashed SourceLocation, never a person, so what is described is exactly the text. And one assistant's opinion is model output, which Invariant 7 says is never evidence by itself, so a note reaches the page only once independent principals agree. Article XVIII is the reason to be strict rather than cautious: fallacy labelling is a standard partisan weapon."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_vocabulary", "label": "config/fallacies.yml \u2014 a closed vocabulary including FALLACY_FALLACY", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Data like config/topics.yml so adding one is not a code change; no free-text fallacy names ever. FALLACY_FALLACY is in the list deliberately, because it is the mistake the feature invites and should be as nameable as the rest. Two entries must say they overlap with what the ledger already measures: CHERRY_PICKING is what independence groups exist to expose, and APPEAL_TO_AUTHORITY is close to what Article X settles \u2014 a note that duplicates a measurement is weaker than the measurement."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_icons", "label": "Icons with no red, green, ticks or crosses, and never without their name", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cards::Badge's palette is deliberately not borrowed: a badge says where evidence stands and these say nothing about evidence at all. The name appears beside the icon always, because an unlabelled symbol is exactly the thing that gets read as a judgement. Without JavaScript the icon is a plain link to the same definition, so the modal is a convenience and never the only way to read it."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_three_failures", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_vocabulary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_icons", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_three_failures", "target": "app_services_reviews_consensus_consensus", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_vocabulary", "target": "app_services_topics_topics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_vocabulary", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_topic_vocabulary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_stage", "target": "app_services_ledger_apply_apply", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_29_fallacy_notes_stage", "target": "app_services_tasks_types_types", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-29-fallacy-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_pl